cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pydemi, please cite it as below."
title: "pydemi: interpretable, fixed-length descriptors from a VASP CHGCAR"
version: 0.2.1
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-28
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22995680
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22995680
    description: "All versions of pydemi"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23664506
    description: "pydemi 0.2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CMSLabIITK/pydemi"
abstract: >-
  pydemi turns the charge density in a VASP CHGCAR into 56 named,
  physically interpretable descriptors in three domains (bonding, structural
  and site heterogeneity), each registered with its formula, units, range and
  fallback values. A graphical interface (pydemi gui) shows the structure,
  density slices, the descriptors and a plot for each. Without a DFT
  calculation, the density can be predicted from the structure with
  ChargE3Net (optional).
